al emergencies (Josh. 18:26; Judg. 20:1, 3; 21:1, 5; 1 Sam. 7:5-16).","verses":30,"v":[1,5,8]},{"id":"bethel_202","name":"Bethel","kind":"","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"A place in Central Palestine, about 10 miles north of Jerusalem, at the head of the pass of Michmash and Ai. It was originally the royal Canaanite city of Luz (Gen. 28:19).","verses":62,"v":[2,19]},{"id":"jabesh-gilead_611","name":"Jabesh-gilead","kind":"City","lat":32.37982,"lon":35.61159,"summary":"A town on the east of Jordan, on the top of one of the green hills of Gilead, within the limits of the half tribe of Manasseh, and in full view of Beth-shan.","verses":12,"v":[8,9,10,12,14]},{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[12]},{"id":"shiloh_1081","name":"Shiloh","kind":"City","lat":32.05617,"lon":35.28988,"summary":"Generally understood as denoting the Messiah, “the peaceful one,” as the word signifies (Gen. 49:10). The Vulgate Version translates the word, “he who is to be sent,” in allusion to the Messiah; the Revised Version, margin, “till he come to Shiloh;” and the LXX., “until that which is his shall come to Shiloh.”","verses":30,"v":[12,19,21]},{"id":"rimmon_1003","name":"Rimmon","kind":"","lat":31.93466,"lon":35.29706,"summary":"“Rock of,” to which the Benjamites fled (Judg. 20:45, 47; 21:13), and where they maintained themselves for four months after the fearful battle at Gibeah, in which they were almost exterminated, 600 only surviving out of about 27,000.","verses":3,"v":[13]},{"id":"lebonah_724","name":"Lebonah","kind":"City","lat":32.07077,"lon":35.23987,"summary":"Frankincense, a town near Shiloh, on the north side of Bethel (Judg. 21:19).","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"shechem_1069","name":"Shechem","kind":"City","lat":32.22111,"lon":35.25444,"summary":"A city in Samaria (Gen. 33:18), called also Sichem (12:6), Sychem (Acts 7:16). It stood in the narrow sheltered valley between Ebal on the north and Gerizim on the south, these mountains at their base being only some 500 yards apart.","verses":40,"v":[19]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC"],"tags":{"bsb":[[376,376,376,3478,3478,7650,7650,7650,7650,4709,4709,559,376,376,4480,4480,1323,1323,1323,1323,5414,5414,1144,1144,1144],[5971,5971,5971,935,1008,1008,3427,3427,8033,6440,430,5704,6153,5375,5375,6963,6963,1058,1058,1419],[4100,3068,3068,430,3478,3478,559,559,559,2063,2063,1961,3478,3478,3117,3478,3478,259,7626,6485,6485],[4283,4283,4283,5971,5971,7925,7925,7925,1129,4196,4196,8033,5927,5927,5930,5930,8002,8002,8002],[1121,1121,559,4310,3605,3605,7626,7626,3478,3478,3808,3808,5927,6951,6951,6951,413,3068,3068,3588,1961,1961,1961,1419,1419,7621,834,834,3808,3808,5927,5927,5927,413,3068,3068,4709,4709,4191,4191,4191,4191,4191,4191],[1121,1121,1121,5162,413,251,251,1144,1144,559,559,3117,259,7626,1438,1438,1438,3478,3478],[4100,6213,6213,6213,802,802,3498,3498,3498,587,587,7650,7650,3068,3068,3068,1115,5414,5414,0,1323,1323,802,802],[559,559,559,4310,259,7626,7626,7626,3478,3478,3808,5927,5927,5927,413,3068,3068,4709,4709,2009,2009,2009,3808,3808,3003,3003,935,935,413,4264,4264,6951,6951,6951],[5971,5971,5971,5971,6485,6485,369,3427,3427,3427,3003,3003,8033,8033],[5712,5712,5712,7971,8147,1121,2428,2428,2428,376,6680,6680,6680,1980,5221,5221,2719,2719,2719,3427,3427,3003,3003,802,802,2945,2945],[2088,834,834,6213,6213,6213,6213,2763,2763,2763,3605,2145,3605,3605,3605,3605,802,3045,3045,3045,3045,3045,2145,2145],[4672,4672,4672,3427,3427,3427,3003,3003,702,3967,5291,1330,834,3808,3808,3045,3045,3045,2145,2145,935,935,935,853,413,4264,4264,7887,7887,776,776,776,3667,3667],[3605,3605,3605,5712,7971,1696,1696,7965,7965,413,1121,1121,834,5553,5553,5553,5553,7417,7417],[1931,1931,1931,6256,1144,1144,7725,5414,5414,5414,802,802,2421,2421,2421,